# Dependencies
node_modules/

# NOTE: docs/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds the built app, and GitHub
# Pages serves the site from there. Committing a build artifact is normally
# poor practice, but here the repo doubles as the host — and the full source
# sits alongside it, so the AGPL's "preferred form for making modifications"
# is unambiguously present.

# Superseded output locations
argument-mapper-public.html
collab-site/

# Your Firebase project id. Not a secret (the security rules are what protect
# the data), but there is no reason for forks to inherit it — they should run
# `firebase use --add` with their own project.
.firebaserc

# Local demo server state (serve.py writes this)
demo-doc.json

# Internal planning/decision notes — not part of the published work
COLLABORATION-HANDOFF-r26.md

# YOUR PRIVATE WORKING NOTES. Keep this rule: a bare `git add .` would
# otherwise publish them to the world.
*.docx
*.doc
*.pages

# Firebase CLI deploy cache
.firebase/

# Superseded releases kept locally for reference. Only the current source
# (argument-mapper-r27.html) is published; the repo's own commit history is
# the record from here on.
argument mapper deprecated/
argument-mapper.html
argument-mapper-r22.html
argument-mapper-r23.html
argument-mapper-r24.html
argument-mapper-r25.html
argument-mapper-r26.html
*.zip

